From 7fa0d76ab1ad45d4fe7a4fbfc50405477ff4ff9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: facetimehd downstream <facetimehd-downstream@localhost>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 15/21] v4l2: deliver the frame rate S_PARM asks for

The sensor runs at one rate. Produce slower rates by delivering one
frame in N and handing the rest straight back to the ISP from a work
item, so G_PARM always reports exactly what the stream delivers and
S_PARM works while streaming. Enumerate frame intervals as the matching
1/30..30/30 stepwise range.

Hold the ISP's AE frame-rate window at 30 fps rather than deriving it
from S_PARM: lowering it is not shown to change the delivered rate, and
a reported rate the stream does not match stalls GStreamer's
pipewiresrc.
